    "text_full": "GitHub Press Biography LinkedIn Twitter Newsletter Blog\nAddy Osmani\nSenior engineering leader and thinker\nAddy Osmani is an Irish Software Engineer and leader currently working as a director at Google Cloud AI, focused on helping developers and businesses succeed with Gemini, Vertex AI, and the Agent Development Kit (ADK). After nearly 14 years leading developer experiences in Chrome, where he worked on DevTools, Lighthouse, and Core Web Vitals, he now bridges Google DeepMind, engineering, product, and developer relations teams. A developer for 25+ years at Google, he is passionate about AI-assisted engineering and developer tools. He previously worked on Fortune 500 sites. Addy is the author of a number of books including Learning JavaScript Design Patterns, Leading Effective Engineering Teams, Stoic Mind and Image Optimization. You can find his open-source work. You can find him on LinkedIn, Twitter or TikTok. He's given over 175 talks worldwide. You can find Addy's writing on his blog, Substack and on LeadDev.\nBooks\nWeb Performance Engineering\nThe Effective Software Engineer\nBeyond Vibe Coding\nEffective Software Engineering Management\nBuilding Web Apps with Bolt\nBuilding large-scale web apps\nEffective Eng. Teams\nProduct Engineering with AI\nJS Patterns: 2nd Edition\nLearning Patterns\nSuccess at Scale\nDeveloper Experience\nThe Stoic Mind\nSoftEng - The Soft Parts\nImage Optimization\nJS Design Patterns\nFeatured: SM Book 4\nBackbone Applications\nCase Studies\neBay\nNetflix\nTinder\nPinterest\nTreebo\nYouTube\nAdobe\nTwitter\nFeatured AI articles\nThe Factory Model: How Coding Agents Changed Software Engineering\nStop Using /init for AGENTS.md\nClaude Code Swarms\nAgentic Engineering\nSelf-Improving Coding Agents\nHow to write a good spec for AI agents\nYour AI coding agents need a manager\nAI writes code faster. Your job is still to prove it works.\nThe Next Two Years of Software Engineering\nMy LLM coding workflow going into 2026\nThe 70% Problem in AI Coding\nMaximizing the Human 30%\nMCP: The Model Context Protocol\nWhy I Use Cline for AI Engineering\nLeading Engineering Teams in the GenAI Era\nAvoiding Skill Atrophy in the Age of AI\nVibe Coding is not an excuse for low-quality work\nWhat are AI Agents? why do they matter?\nVibe Coding: Revolution or Reckless Abandon?\nAI-Driven Prototyping: v0, Bolt, and Lovable Compareda\n\n \n\nFeatured thoughts\nCritical Thinking is key\nOvercome team dysfunction\nWork is a subset of life\nCoach, mentor, sponsor\nEffective engineers\n\nCheck out more of my thoughts on LinkedIn.\n\n\t\nCurrent projects\n\nI am a director at Google Cloud AI, focused on helping developers and businesses succeed with Gemini, Vertex AI, and the Agent Development Kit (ADK). I bridge Google DeepMind, engineering, product, go-to-market, and developer relations teams. After nearly 14 years leading developer experiences in Chrome, where I worked on DevTools, Lighthouse, and Core Web Vitals, I'm now focused on enterprise AI. I also love side-projects.\n\n\n\n\t\nOpen-source\n\nProjects I've contributed to include Lighthouse, Workbox, Quicklink, Guess.js, Yeoman, TodoMVC, Speedometer, Critical and Material Design Lite. You can find more on my open-source page or on GitHub.\n\n\n\n\t\nPodcasts\n\nI have been on a few different podcasts recently, including PodRocket, Hanselminutes with Scott Hanselman, DevDiscuss and Smashing Podcast.\n\n\n\n\t\nTalks\n\nRecordings of my talks are on my YouTube channel. These include Optimize the Core Web Vitals and Cost Of JavaScript. You can find some of my slides on SpeakerDeck.\n\n\n\n\t\nBlog\n\nYou can find my writing on my blog, Substack and on LeadDev. My last post on here was: Don't Outsource the Learning\n\nFeatured Videos\nBeyond Vibe Coding\nThe AI-Assisted Developer Workflow\nHow to become a \"T-shaped\" software engineer\nLife Lessons\nEffective Engineering Teams\nCost Of JavaScript\n\nCheck out more of my videos on YouTube.\n\nShorts